  "$sharedHubsNote": "frontend/src/i18n/messages/*.json is a shared hub under protest, not by design. Localization is a standing rule, so a track that could not edit the catalogs could not finish a UI change — but the store is partitioned by LOCALE, a presentation axis, so no bounded context owns its own vocabulary. A track appends only under its own DOMAIN namespace (commerce.*, growth.*, canvas.* — the same boundary schema/<domain>.ts draws) and serializes. ROADMAP W0-2 repartitions the source by domain (messages/<domain>/{en,zh,es,fr,de}.json, folded into the existing per-locale published asset by frontend/scripts/publish-message-catalogs.mjs); when it lands, remove this entry from sharedHubs and give each lane its own directory."
